<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The one entitlement a signed build asks for: the domain whose https sign-in handoff this
  app may receive.

  Approved by Tadas on 2026-09-13 (AGENTS.md, "The phone signs in through the web sign-in").
  Apple verifies it by fetching /.well-known/apple-app-site-association from that host, which
  is what stops another app on the phone claiming a Motet sign-in — the weakness a custom URL
  scheme cannot close.

  **Deliberately not Motet.entitlements**, which asks for `com.apple.developer.carplay-audio`.
  That one is granted by Apple's manual review, and an ungranted entitlement fails a build to
  *sign* rather than merely lacking the feature. These two must stay in separate files until
  CarPlay is granted.

  The domain is a build setting rather than a literal: this repo is public and names no
  deployment's hosts. `ios/bin/testflight upload` passes it from the `testflight`
  environment's MOTET_IOS_APP_DOMAIN, and a build without that setting must not point
  CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS here — `applinks:` with nothing after it is not a domain.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:$(MOTET_APP_LINK_DOMAIN)</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
